ues/comments/219806557","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/1172#issuecomment-219806557","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/1172","id":219806557,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIxOTgwNjU1Nw==","user":{"login":"wittekm","id":578530,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3ODUzMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/578530?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wittekm","html_url":"https://github.com/wittekm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wittekm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wittekm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wittekm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wittekm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wittekm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wittekm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wittekm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wittekm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wittekm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-05-17T18:16:39Z","updated_at":"2016-05-17T18:16:39Z","body":"Still not fully supported - see [Jukka's comment on the pull request](https://github.com/python/mypy/pull/1535#issuecomment-219790552) - but better than it was before.\n\nIs there any unhacky way to do this in the future? Enum is implemented with [an overridden `__getattr__` on the class object](https://hg.python.org/cpython/file/3.5/Lib/enum.py), which shadows its true members. That is to say, SomeEnum.x calls getattr, not the member 'x' of SomeEnum.\n\nI'm not sure if MyPy supports typing on `__getattr__`, but even if it did, there would have to be some sort of placeholder type that changes for each subclass, like\n\n```\ndef __getattr__(cls, name: str) -> WhateverClsIs\n```\n\nI don't have an in-depth background in type theory, but this probably breaks every convention :(\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/219806557/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"wittekm","id":578530,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU3ODUzMA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/578530?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wittekm","html_url":"https://github.com/wittekm","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wittekm/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wittekm/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wittekm/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wittekm/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wittekm/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wittekm/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wittekm/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wittekm/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wittekm/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/219808784","html_url":"https://github.com/python/mypy/issues/1172#issuecomment-219808784","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/1172","id":219808784,"node_id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDIxOTgwODc4NA==","user":{"login":"gvanrossum","id":2894642,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4OTQ2NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2894642?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum","html_url":"https://github.com/gvanrossum","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2016-05-17T18:24:17Z","updated_at":"2016-05-17T18:24:17Z","body":"At issue here seems to be that Enum does some very clever things to change the semantics of assignments in the class body. Those clever things are mostly hidden from the type checker, which has a much more \"naive\" view of the world than what's actually possible in Python. If this hackery were a third-party package we would probably say \"too bad\" and recommend a clunkier way to spell it; given that it's in the stdlib we're trying to make mypy support it as well as we can. But it's unrealistic to expect mypy to understand the `__getattr__` implementation on the metaclass. (Halting problem anyone? :-)\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/python/mypy/issues/comments/219808784/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"gvanrossum","id":2894642,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI4OTQ2NDI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2894642?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum","html_url":"https://github.com/gvanrossum","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/gvanrossum/starred{/owner}{/repo}"